# Build context for the web and migration images (context = repo root).
#
# The first block is the one that matters: a build context is copied into the
# daemon wholesale, and anything that lands in a layer is readable by anyone who
# can pull the image. Real credentials live in .env / .env.local on a developer
# machine, so they are excluded here as well as in .gitignore — the two files
# protect against different accidents and neither substitutes for the other.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Never needed at build time, and a large context is a slow one.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
dist
build
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Documentation and infrastructure are not inputs to an application image.
docs
infra
*.md
!apps/web/AGENTS.md

# The Python service builds from its own context (services/face-ai).
services

# Local tooling and OS noise.
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.log
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv
